# Resume Mission reprograms the mission from a waypoint, then (copter) Guided, arm, take off, Auto.
#
# BUT_resumemis_Click: a warning, then "Resume mission at waypoint#" (lastautowp, or 1), then the
# vehicle's mission is read, everything before the waypoint except home, takeoffs and the "do"
# commands is dropped, the rest is written back and read into the planner, waypoint 1 is made
# current, and on a copter the vehicle is put in Guided, armed and told to take off to the
# waypoint's height before Auto. `GCSViews/FlightData.cs:1481-1627`
#
# The five-item mission below resumed at 4 keeps home, the takeoff and the DO_CHANGE_SPEED and
# drops waypoint 2: four items.
#
# On ArduCopter the resume ends in "Command Failed", as Mission Planner's does. The C# sends the
# TAKEOFF, sleeps a second, and sends it again until the vehicle is within 2 m of the waypoint's
# height, and a TAKEOFF refused is "Command Failed" and the end of it
# (`GCSViews/FlightData.cs:1587-1605`). ArduCopter refuses every take-off once the vehicle has
# left the ground (`Mode::do_user_takeoff_U_m`: "can't takeoff again!"), and 8 m at 2.5 m/s is
# more than three seconds' climb, so one of the repeats is always refused - the runs of
# 2026-09-24 16:36 and 16:38 said so. The vehicle, armed in Guided, climbs on to the first
# take-off's 10 m, and Auto is never asked for. `fly.rs`'s
# `the_resume_script_expects_what_the_csharp_leaves_on_arducopter` checks the expectations below
# against a model of that, and `resume_sitl.rs` has the repeated take-off against SITL itself.
# Then it lands the vehicle and waits for it to disarm.
#
# THIS FLIES SITL: it arms and climbs. Needs a copter SITL:
#   tools/gui-test.sh tests/gui/fly-resumemis.gui -- tcp:127.0.0.1:5760
# The setup writes the mission through SITL's second port, 5762.

setup printf 'QGC WPL 110\n0\t1\t0\t16\t0\t0\t0\t0\t-35.363262\t149.165237\t584.09\t1\n1\t0\t3\t22\t0\t0\t0\t0\t0\t0\t10\t1\n2\t0\t3\t16\t0\t0\t0\t0\t-35.3629\t149.165237\t10\t1\n3\t0\t3\t178\t0\t5\t0\t0\t0\t0\t0\t1\n4\t0\t3\t16\t0\t0\t0\t0\t-35.3625\t149.1657\t10\t1\n' > $WORK/mission.waypoints
setup cargo run -q -p mp-cli --bin headless-planner -- mission tcp:127.0.0.1:5762 $WORK/mission.waypoints

screen fly
window 1600x1200
settle 8

# The Actions grid is on the Actions page, tabActions; the strip opens on Quick, as
# tabControlactions.SelectedIndex = 0 has it. `GCSViews/FlightData.Designer.cs:595-611`
click fly-tab-actions
expect fly.tab tabActions

expect vehicle.armed false
expect fly.resume idle

click fly-resumemis
settle 1
expect fly.prompt ~ Warning this will reprogram your mission, arm and issue a takeoff command
click fly-prompt-ok
settle 1
# lastautowp is -1 until the vehicle has flown in Auto, so the box offers 1.
expect fly.prompt ~ Resume mission at waypoint
key ctrl+u
type 4
# Keystrokes reach the application through the input method (ibus, over XIM) and come back
# after a round trip; a click does not. Settle, so the click cannot overtake the typing.
settle 1
click fly-prompt-ok
settle 12

# Home is not a row: resuming at 4 keeps the takeoff, the speed change and waypoint 4.
expect mission.items 3
# Armed in Guided, the first take-off accepted and a repeat of it refused.
expect vehicle.armed true
expect vehicle.mode Guided
expect fly.sent COMMAND_LONG MAV_CMD_NAV_TAKEOFF 0,0,0,0,0,0,10
expect fly.ack MAV_CMD_NAV_TAKEOFF: failed
expect fly.resume failed: The Command failed to execute

# Down again.
click land
settle 30
expect vehicle.armed false

# Landed, the vehicle is left in Stabilize, as the next test finds a fresh SITL: Land is not a
# mode a copter arms in, and a vehicle left there fails every later arming check.
click Stabilize
settle 2
expect vehicle.mode Stabilize
